  "reconstructibility": 0,
  "reason": "R2 directly establishes short-range ordering in the same W-Ta-Cr-V refractory alloy and uses a DFT-derived cluster expansion for efficient sampling, while R4 and R10 establish temperature-dependent SRO in the closely related W-Ta-Cr-V-Hf system. Several other records provide only general support for chemical ordering, electronic effects, or Gibbs-energy-based phase stability. None describes a machine-learning interatomic potential, matching an ML potential to the DFT phase-space distribution, free-energy perturbation as a replacement for thermodynamic integration, liquid free-energy or melting-point calculations, or the small MTP–DFT energy-difference variance needed for rapid FEP convergence. Thus, despite prior evidence that SRO matters in this alloy family, the records do not point toward the later paper's combined MTP/FEP intervention or its melting-temperature mechanism."
